            <ArticleTitle>[Pericardial cyst--a rare cause of thoracic pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a 10 cm in diameter and 450 ml large pericardial coelom cyst causing chest pain in a previously healthy 38-year-old man is reported. The cyst was diagnosed by transthoracic echocardiography and computerized tomography. The patient recovered without complications following surgical removal of the cyst.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
